> > >> provided you didn't snack anything in between.
> 
> > > Or save the game and restart.
> 
> > Whoops! I didn't know that. I always assumed that saving the game changed
> > nothing in the current game state.
> 
> IIRC, saving the game also makes it forget how much the stats have been
> exercised / abused since the last check.

No. It will forget when the next check was due, and fake up a
plausible value on restore, but the exercises and abuses themselves
are stored in the u.aexe.a[] array and thus remembered.

(There's quite a lot of state variables that aren't persistent across
saves; the 'victual' struct and 'next_check' are just two examples. In
some cases, such as 'unweapon', this is actually the Right Thing: you
_should_ get another "You begin bashing monsters with" message in a
new session, in case you'd forgotten.)

